From 95fac465708acad705280fa88565bb60462b16c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: YamadaBlog <118530756+YamadaBlog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 16:36:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 25/27] Niri gesture: leaving a column takes the same gesture
 whatever its width

Snap used the snap point nearest to the projected position, and neighbouring points are a column
width apart: leaving a full-width column needed ~1033 pt of projected travel against ~516 pt for a
half-width one. From the point the strip rested on, a projected travel past halfway to the next
point, capped at a quarter of the viewport, now goes to that point (further if the projection
reaches further); shorter travel returns. Narrow and half-width columns are unchanged.
